diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c56a1c289341cfb97081c0ea58b78da1c353a8eb..0564ab28d64d79609a35c4c4fb928b5f75f4ee27 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,13 +4,25 @@ Infrastructure for the Vancouver Linux Users Group.
 
 ## Overview
 
-🚧 This project is a work-in-progress! Instructions will be added as soon as it is usable. 🚧
+This repo contains all infrastructure as code definitions (as OpenTofu, Ansible and rootless Podman Quadlets hardened with SELinux/gVisor) for VanLUG, including:
+
+- The VanLUG [Forgejo](https://forgejo.org/) instance
+- A [Forgejo runner](https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/actions/#forgejo-runner) instance using gVisor to run semi-untrusted code
+- [Caddy](https://caddyserver.com/) as the reverse proxy, with [firewalld](https://firewalld.org/) as the firewall and [Anubis](https://anubis.techaro.lol/) to prevent the Forgejo instance from being overloaded by scrapers
+- [git-pages](https://git-pages.org/) to host the VanLUG website and any members website
+- A custom Podman quadlet for the VanLUG API, which powers e.g. the Luma and Mastodon proxies
+
+## Acknowledgements
+
+- [eriksjolund/podman-caddy-socket-activation](https://github.com/eriksjolund/podman-caddy-socket-activation) and [eriksjolund/podman-nginx-socket-activation](https://github.com/eriksjolund/podman-nginx-socket-activation) provide the socket activation patterns for the Caddy reverse proxy and its upstreams
 
 ## Contributing
 
-To contribute, please use the [Codeberg flow](https://docs.codeberg.org/collaborating/) and follow our [Code of Conduct](./CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
+Contributions to this repository are restricted to the VanLUG technical comittee at this time.
 
-To deploy the infrastructure locally, run:
+To contribute, please use the [Codeberg flow](https://docs.codeberg.org/collaborating/) and follow our [Code of Conduct](https://vanlug.p8.lu/conduct/).
+
+To deploy the infrastructure locally, first use [OpenTofu](https://opentofu.org/) to create the physical infrastructure by running the following:
 
 ```shell
 $ git clone https://codeberg.org/pojntfx/vanlug-infrastructure
@@ -18,8 +30,24 @@ $ cd vanlug-infrastructure
 $ source .env.local # See `.env` for required secrets; ask `@pojntfx:beeper.com` for access
 $ tofu init
 $ tofu apply
+```
+
+Then, to use [Ansible](https://docs.ansible.com/projects/ansible/latest/index.html) to provision the hosts, run:
+
+```shell
 $ ansible-galaxy collection install cloud.terraform ansible.posix community.general community.docker
-$ ansible-playbook site.yaml # You might want to change `binary_path` in `inventory.yaml` first
+$ ANSIBLE_CONFIG=config/ansible.cfg ansible-playbook site.yaml # You might want to change `binary_path` in `inventory.yaml` first
+```
+
+Once the hosts are provisioned, sign into Forgejo, [import](https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/user/repo-mirror/) the VanLUG website repo from the [GitHub mirror](https://github.com/vanlug/vanlug.github.io), wait for the actions to pass (which build the website and API), and provision the quadlet for the API (the website is automatically deployed using [git-pages](https://git-pages.org/):
+
+```shell
+$ ANSIBLE_CONFIG=config/ansible.cfg ansible-playbook playbooks/vanlug-api.yaml # You might want to change `binary_path` in `inventory.yaml` first
+```
+
+Everything should now be up and running, and auto-updates should be enabled for all components, including the quadlets and OS itself. To get logs, run the following:
+
+```shell
 # To get logs for quadlets on main server
 $ ssh setup@vanlug.p8.lu
 [setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo journalctl -u caddy.service -f
@@ -32,12 +60,14 @@ $ ssh setup@2a01:4f8:c015:706c::1
 [setup@vanlug-forgejo-runner ~]$ sudo journalctl _SYSTEMD_USER_UNIT=forgejo-runner.service -f
 ```
 
-To update the SELinux policies for the containers (`.cil` files), run:
+That's it! All infrastructure should now be deployed.
+
+During development, to update the SELinux policies for the containers (`.cil` files), run:
 
 ```shell
 $ ssh setup@vanlug.p8.lu
 [setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo -iu caddy podman inspect caddy | sudo udica caddy
-$ scp setup@vanlug.p8.lu:/home/setup/caddy.cil caddy.cil
+$ scp setup@vanlug.p8.lu:/home/setup/caddy.cil policies/caddy.cil
 ```
 
 You'll then need to manually edit the CIL file (see https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux-notebook/blob/main/src/cil_overview.md and https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux/tree/master/secilc/docs for a guide) for any additional capabilities the container might need. You can see the denials by running the following:
@@ -56,8 +86,8 @@ $ cd forgejo/
 $ # Both the icon and logo of these must be square
 $ curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vanlug/vanlug.github.io/refs/heads/main/static/design/icon.svg | tee ./assets/favicon.svg ./assets/logo.svg > /dev/null
 $ make generate-images
-$ mkdir -p ../custom/public/assets/img/
-$ cp public/assets/img/{logo.svg,logo.png,avatar_default.png,repo_default.png,apple-touch-icon.png,favicon.svg,favicon.png} ../custom/public/assets/img/
+$ mkdir -p ../config/custom/public/assets/img/
+$ cp public/assets/img/{logo.svg,logo.png,avatar_default.png,repo_default.png,apple-touch-icon.png,favicon.svg,favicon.png} ../config/custom/public/assets/img/
 ```
 
 ## License
